# The BEAM gate's container, plus a Python the differential harness can use.
#
# Why this exists: `beam/apps/vitrial_sync/test/support/` contains a differential
# harness that AST-lifts the Python reference out of `app/`, executes it, and
# compares the answers against the Elixir. That harness is the only thing making
# the parity claims in ARCHITECTURE.md §2.1 mean anything — but the pinned
# hexpm/elixir slim image ships NO python3, so in that image the harness skips
# itself and `mix test` reports 532 passed with 23 skipped. A gate that skips its
# own oracle is a gate that cannot fail, which is the exact defect class this
# repository has been closing all along.
#
# So the gate image is the pinned BEAM image plus python3 and pydantic. Nothing
# else changes: same OTP, same Elixir, same Debian release, so the compile and
# the 532 existing tests are the same tests the CI job runs. This ADDS the
# ability to execute the oracle; it does not relax anything.
#
# Build:  podman build -t server-api-beam-gate:local -f beam/Dockerfile.gate .
# The gate script builds this on demand and falls back to the base image with a
# loud warning when it cannot, so an offline host still gets format+compile+test.
#
# WAVE 5 CAVEAT, ON THE RECORD: with epgsql admitted (beam/mix.lock is live),
# that fallback promise has narrowed. The BASE image ships no Hex and no package
# cache, so on a fully-offline host whose cached gate image is ABSENT, the
# fallback lane cannot resolve the dependency and the gate cannot run. The bake
# below exists precisely so the normal lane — the gate image, built once with
# network — never reaches hex.pm again at run time.
FROM docker.io/hexpm/elixir:1.20.4-erlang-29.1.1-debian-bookworm-20260918-slim

# python3: the harness's interpreter. pydantic: the reference's own dependency,
# and without it every oracle call fails in a way that looks like a parity
# mismatch rather than a missing module.
RUN apt-get update \
 && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends python3 python3-pip \
 && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

RUN pip3 install --no-cache-dir --break-system-packages "pydantic>=2,<3"

# The Hex provisioning, baked as a MECHANISM (archive + package cache in the
# image), not asserted as an outcome. Before wave 5 the gate had zero hex deps,
# so the base image needed nothing; with beam/mix.lock live, `mix deps.get` at
# gate time needs Hex itself plus the resolved package bytes. This is an
# offline-verification shape, not a shortcut: beam_gate.sh still runs
# `mix local.hex --if-missing && mix deps.get` in every lane, and ci.yml's
# umbrella job rebuilds THIS Dockerfile and does the same — the cache just makes
# those commands no-ops. Requires network at IMAGE BUILD time (once).
#
# The scratch tree is the minimal umbrella a resolve needs: the root mix.exs
# (apps_path), the one app that declares the dep, and the committed lock —
# `mix deps.get` then resolves byte-exactly what CI will verify against that
# same lock. The scratch tree is discarded; ~/.hex (cache.ets + the epgsql tar)
# and ~/.mix/archives (hex, rebar3) are what persist.
RUN mix local.hex --force \
 && mix local.rebar --force

# Dependency pre-seed. OPTIONAL by design, and the previous version of this file
# was not: it did `COPY beam/mix.exs beam/mix.lock`, which fails the whole build
# with
#
#   failed to calculate checksum ...: "/beam/mix.lock": not found
#
# the moment the lockfile is deleted. That is exactly what happened when the
# maintainer ruled "native as much as possible" and epgsql was removed — the
# lockfile went, and this line took the whole gate image down with it. A
# dependency-cache line must not be load-bearing on the dependency existing.
#
# The lockfile is copied with a GLOB, and that is the whole mechanism: Docker's
# COPY fails on a literal path that does not exist, but a wildcard that matches
# nothing copies nothing and succeeds. Putting `COPY beam/mix.lock` on its own
# line does NOT work — verified, it fails the build identically.
COPY beam/mix.exs /tmp/depseed/
# Every app that declares a dependency needs its mix.exs in the seed tree, or
# the baked cache silently lacks its packages: `mix deps.get` resolves the UNION
# of the copied apps' deps, so a cache seeded from vitrial_sync alone (whose
# deps list is empty since the epgsql hand-rewrite) contains no cowboy -- and an
# offline host whose gate image predates the dep is stuck at beam_gate.sh's
# exit 5. Wave 6 admitted cowboy in vitrial_web, so its mix.exs is seeded too;
# add the next app's line when the next dependency lands.
COPY beam/apps/vitrial_sync/mix.exs /tmp/depseed/apps/vitrial_sync/mix.exs
COPY beam/apps/vitrial_web/mix.exs /tmp/depseed/apps/vitrial_web/mix.exs
COPY beam/mix.* /tmp/depseed/

RUN cd /tmp/depseed \
 && mix deps.get \
 && cd / \
 && rm -rf /tmp/depseed